NOTE, and it is the reason this table is small print: the export is set by
the TOP interface, where the shape is anchored at f = 1. So K(z) as
parameterised here does NOT reduce the required export at fixed kz -- it
only does so by letting kz itself be smaller. Read the kz axis, not the
z_K axis. If the best A configuration wants a LARGER kz, candidate A makes
the pump's export problem WORSE, not better, and the two are then in
tension rather than complementary -- which would correct DESIGN sec.3.4a.


