--- the rows-4-and-5 prediction, scored ---
A and B1 move the DIC gradient by at most 0.00e+00 umol/kg and the
d13C gradient by at most 2.22e-13 permil. Predicted: EXACTLY ZERO, by
conservation -- neither tracer has an interior source, so any steady state
of any transport operator is uniform in ratio.
VERDICT: CONFIRMED. Transport CANNOT produce the observed interior gradients.


=== PART 5. THE DECISION RULE, SCORED ===
candidate A  best |z| at matched sink: 0.17  (z_K = 5000, kz = 6404, d logL +0.9)
candidate B1 best |z|:                 2.26  (SH only 0.5, d logL +0.1)
incumbent    |z|:                      1.70

RULE FIRES: a one-knob transport fix reaches |z| < 1 AT MATCHED SINK.
The deep-D14C deficit is STRUCTURAL -- a single diffusive column with a
depth-DEPENDENT K reaches the target that the same column with a constant
K cannot. B2 is NOT indicated by this result.
BUT READ CLAUSE 1 BEFORE CONCLUDING: the h_ml profile above is what says
whether the winner also supplies what h_ml = 184 m is faking, and a
candidate that fixes clause 3 while leaving clause 1 untouched has solved
one of the two things the ocean structure is wanted for, not both.
AND NOTE HOW LITTLE THE OBJECTIVE CARES: over the iso-sink rows the logL
spread from z_K Inf to z_K 3000 is ~2 units while deep D14C moves ~3.5
sigma. That is the deep-D14C term's sigma (10.3 permil at n_eff = 20)
doing exactly what it should -- a 1.9 sigma gain IS only ~1.4 log-units --
but it means z_K would be WEAKLY IDENTIFIED in a refit, and how weakly is
set by the GLODAP n_eff choice that build_glodap_deep_targets.R flagged as
UNRESOLVED. Adopting A puts weight on that unresolved choice.

AND INDEPENDENT OF WHICH: rows 4 and 5 are untouchable by transport, so the
pump is NOT in competition with A, B1 or B2. The question was never which
candidate; it is which COMBINATION, and the objective cannot currently see
two of the five rows at all.


